# The Content-Security-Policy in Caddyfile.prod carries a sha256 of the inline
# theme-boot script in apps/web/index.html (see F-004 there), and a browser
# hashes the exact bytes it receives. With git's default autocrlf those bytes
# are CRLF in a Windows checkout and LF in the Linux build that actually
# ships -- two different hashes for one script, so the policy would be right
# on one platform and silently wrong on the other.
#
# Pinning the file to LF makes the hash machine-independent, which is what
# lets the hash be a committed constant that a test can check rather than
# something regenerated per build.
apps/web/index.html text eol=lf
